{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1005938-solars-the-thousand-streams-river","id":1005938,"title":"Solars & the Thousand Streams River","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-20T19:04:39-08:00","id":1005938,"title":"Solars & the Thousand Streams River","content":"Say a circle of Solars somehow gets in good with Lunars of the Winding Path and try to support their efforts to build societies that can survive and thrive without the Exalted: how does that play out? What kind of society would a Solar/Lunar collaboration produce?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1448-william-louison","name":"William Louison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T19:21:22-08:00","id":1005941,"title":"","content":"Assuming 2e? A dead one, because elder Sidereal strike teams would kill them with their broken martial arts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T20:21:52-08:00","id":1005954,"title":"","content":"For the sake of argument, let's assume Zero Dark Sidereal isn't a concern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1448-william-louison","name":"William Louison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T20:25:46-08:00","id":1005956,"title":"","content":"I think that would depend heavily on the solars and lunars in question. Just about anything is possible, from a autocratic society built on sorcery and slave labor to a neo-pagan utopia built around deals with the local gods and spirits.<br /> <br /> The only thing that these societies have in common is access to substantial magic that does not involve the Exalted. That one trait is really the only qualification a society needs to be a Thousand Streams River Project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 11-21-2016, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T20:44:58-08:00","id":1005962,"title":"","content":"I think this would be super doable as long as the society was able to protect itself from the more powerful beings that the setting is full of. I would say with beuracracy charms from an eclipse and getting a good dojo going capable of training up a samurai like class as well as a scholar/witch doctor class it should work. It would be pretty hands on at first but then totally hands off after awhile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11567-jairain","name":"Jairain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11567_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"345"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T20:56:40-08:00","id":1005967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1005938-solars-the-thousand-streams-river?p=1005956#post1005956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that would depend heavily on the solars and lunars in question. Just about anything is possible, from a autocratic society built on sorcery and slave labor to a neo-pagan utopia built around deals with the local gods and spirits.<br /> <br /> The only thing that these societies have in common is access to substantial magic that does not involve the Exalted. That one trait is really the only qualification is society needs to be a Thousand Streams River Project.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is 2e we're talking about. The only possible outcome is failure, with angry men yelling their mothers' names - which are coincidentally the same - at each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T01:42:09-08:00","id":1006063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>William Louison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1005938-solars-the-thousand-streams-river#post1005938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say a circle of Solars somehow gets in good with Lunars of the Winding Path and try to support their efforts to build societies that can survive and thrive without the Exalted: how does that play out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Badly. Thousand Streams River was always a really bad concept, and one of the things that added to the 2e's theme of &quot;lunars are useless&quot;.<br /> But if you want an ingame example, look at Halta and Linowan. One is a Lunar project, one a Solar creation. There's no meaningful difference between them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T02:02:34-08:00","id":1006069,"title":"","content":"Now this is a distinctly unhelpful thread, isn't it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>William Louison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1005938-solars-the-thousand-streams-river#post1005938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say a circle of Solars somehow gets in good with Lunars of the Winding Path and try to support their efforts to build societies that can survive and thrive without the Exalted: how does that play out? What kind of society would a Solar/Lunar collaboration produce?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSolar Socialize Charms to shape societies would be a significant asset in this kind of strategy. I feel as though when that kind of power is brought into the mx, it just becomes a question of what kind of society the collaboration wants.<br /> <br /> \u200bTaking the premise of the Thousand Streams River at face value, it identified itself as something with no single answer, no distinct formula as to what functioned as a society not run (overtly) by the Exalted. So it really could be almost anything.<br /> <br /> I could picture the form of the collaboration itself being that the Solar is an internal observer and occasional troubleshooter, while the Lunar focuses on eliminating threats from without.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T02:49:51-08:00","id":1006083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1005938-solars-the-thousand-streams-river?p=1005967#post1005967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is 2e we're talking about. The only possible outcome is failure, with angry men yelling their mothers' names - which are coincidentally the same - at each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, so the actual criteria for exaltation is that your mother's name is Martha? All that &quot;you need to be heroic&quot;-stuff is just a giant red herring?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T07:35:52-08:00","id":1006186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1005938-solars-the-thousand-streams-river?p=1006063#post1006063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Badly. Thousand Streams River was always a really bad concept, and one of the things that added to the 2e's theme of &quot;lunars are useless&quot;.<br /> But if you want an ingame example, look at Halta and Linowan. One is a Lunar project, one a Solar creation. There's no meaningful difference between them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Halta was retconned into a Lunar project, and the Linowan only worship the Unconquered Sun because of their beliefs in excellence and bravery. Or did 2e retcon the Linowan, too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T09:41:27-08:00","id":1006239,"title":"","content":"Huh. I haven't followed the forums in years and only just started reading the 2e Lunars book, so I'm curious why the Lunars are seen as useless? <br /> <br /> I think a point of tension for any Solars participating in a Thousand Streams River project would be the temptation, whenever a internal problem or external threat popped up, to handle everything themselves. Solars, more than Lunars, seem like they're prone to being the overprotective parent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1448-william-louison","name":"William Louison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T10:27:16-08:00","id":1006265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>William Louison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1005938-solars-the-thousand-streams-river?p=1006239#post1006239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so I'm curious why the Lunars are seen as useless?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, just the Thousand Streams thing has some evident shortcomings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>William Louison</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a point of tension for any Solars participating in a Thousand Streams River project would be the temptation, whenever a internal problem or external threat popped up, to handle everything themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably no more than it would be for the Lunars themselves.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe whole Thousand Streams bit already implicitly assumes Exalted who don't want to run things directly, or that there's a distinction between this and being responsible for keeping interlopers out, in the first place, so just run with that in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>William Louison</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars, more than Lunars, seem like they're prone to being the overprotective parent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh; plenty of signature characters are quite unlike that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T10:51:41-08:00","id":1006278,"title":"","content":"I feel like this thread is rooted in the assumption that Solars are a demographic group. I don't think it's fair to think of them that way. Although different Solars may have similar abilities, the fact that they can come from any walk of life and are not compelled to have a common culture or ideology makes categorically determining how they would behave a futile exercise. <br /> <br /> Lunars aren't much better in that respect - the Silver pact gives them something like a common culture, but no more than that. They, too, can come from anywhere and do whatever they like. <br /> <br /> Ultimately, I think the kinds of societies they would build together would not necessarily be any different than what they would build apart. So much depends on the temperament and philosophy of the individual people involved, I doubt you can really make any blanket assumptions about what they would do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T11:31:45-08:00","id":1006307,"title":"","content":"My problem with the Thousand Streams River Project is that MoEP: Lunars is adept at ignoring the similarities between it and the Sidereal Exalted modus operandi that people immediately recognise as sinister. Hell, it's endgame feels like something the Bronze Faction could get behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T13:26:34-08:00","id":1006366,"title":"","content":"As a concept, the TSR is fine. You could easily slot it in as a Solar or Sidereal plot (on a small or large scale), because the notion that humanity <i>shouldn't</i> need the Exalted is a broadly appealing one. A philanthropist is a man in the business of putting himself out of business, after all.<br /> <br /> The problem with the TSR is twofold:<br /> <br /> 1. Every Lunar is apparently in on it or at least aware of it? This is dumb.<br /> 2. Everyone with a scrap of magic to their name is better at it than a Lunar.<br /> 2a. The people who would be the very best at it (except for fae, who are best at everything large-scale) are the Solars, the default protagonists of the setting.<br /> <br /> In fact, if I didn't know better, I would say that TSR was made for the specific purpose of letting a circle of social Solars embarrass the hell out of Lunars by accomplishing more in a month than they could in hundreds of years.<br /> <br /> So yeah, by all means get your Solars in on that, it might actually work as a result!<br /> <br /> As for the society it would create... kinda depends on your Solars/Lunars, don't you think? A buddy-cop pair concerned with law and justice would mould a very different autonomous civilization than a pair of warrior-poets who are concerned with grand deeds and martial valor, you know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","user":"Guancyto","date":". 11-21-2016, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T13:37:45-08:00","id":1006375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1005938-solars-the-thousand-streams-river?p=1006307#post1006307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with the Thousand Streams River Project is that MoEP: Lunars is adept at ignoring the similarities between it and the Sidereal Exalted modus operandi that people immediately recognise as sinister.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun little etymology factoid for the day: <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The meaning for &quot;sinister&quot; in the sense of &quot;evil&quot; is a little bit of a drift from the old Latin days when it meant &quot;left.&quot; &quot;Dexter&quot; was &quot;right,&quot; so to be &quot;dextrous&quot; was to be <i>super</i>-right-handed, and to be skilled with both hands was to be &quot;ambidextrous,&quot; as in, &quot;right-handed in both hands.&quot;<br /> <br /> These ramblings brought to you by an early Christmas gift from my little sister; she got me a T-shirt that reads, &quot;I'm left-handed! What's <i>your</i> superpower?&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-21-2016, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T14:51:41-08:00","id":1006407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>William Louison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1005938-solars-the-thousand-streams-river?p=1006239#post1006239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. I haven't followed the forums in years and only just started reading the 2e Lunars book, so I'm curious why the Lunars are seen as useless?</div> </div> </div> </div>There'd been not much mention of Lunar's in EX2 until their splatbook released, which raised the question of &quot;just <i>what</i> have the Lunars been doing from the usurpation till the return?&quot; <i>One </i>of EX2's answer was The Thousand Streams River project and retconning events which had <i>other </i>explanations in earlier books as actually being TSR. This unfortunately gave the <i>impression </i>that the Lunars had only been making the setting look <i>exactly like it would if they weren't there</i>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T11:15:45-08:00","id":1006779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1005938-solars-the-thousand-streams-river?p=1006186#post1006186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Halta was retconned into a Lunar project, and the Linowan only worship the Unconquered Sun because of their beliefs in excellence and bravery. Or did 2e retcon the Linowan, too?</div> </div> </div> </div>If i remember correctly, Linowan in 2e got made into a remains of a First Age social project.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1005938-solars-the-thousand-streams-river?p=1006407#post1006407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There'd been not much mention of Lunar's in EX2 until their splatbook released, which raised the question of &quot;just <i>what</i> have the Lunars been doing from the usurpation till the return?&quot; <i>One </i>of EX2's answer was The Thousand Streams River project and retconning events which had <i>other </i>explanations in earlier books as actually being TSR. This unfortunately gave the <i>impression </i>that the Lunars had only been making the setting look <i>exactly like it would if they weren't there</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Additionally, since TSR was full of fail on many levels, it gave the impression that Lunars spent hundreds of years playing with toys (human toys) for no gain whatsoever, just so they could pretend they're doing something useful.<br /> <br /> The examples we got of TSR projects (with the really standing out exception of Haslanti) didn't help there","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T14:23:49-08:00","id":1006860,"title":"","content":"The TSR was a necessary evil to allow the Lunars to engage in kingdom building in a setting designed around the fact that Lunars were explicitly hunted down and murdered by organized groups of Exalted whenever they tried to engage in overt activities (like engaging in kingdom building). So it was predicated first and foremost on the basic idea that if Lunars wanted to engage in kingdom building, they'd have to do so from behind the scenes. <br /> <br /> It was, to be fair, a step-up from early 1st edition where the answer to, &quot;How do the Lunars engage in kingdom building,&quot; was a flat, &quot;They <b>don't.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> Still, even in 3rd edition where the Thousand Streams River project is no longer a thing, I suspect that most Lunars who do engage in any kind of large-scale kingdom building are going to operate off many of the same basic strategies and assumptions since being an open Anathema trying to conquer or rule a vast empire tends to attract those pesky Wyld Hunts. <br /> <br /> Anyway, back to the OP's topic. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>William Louison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1005938-solars-the-thousand-streams-river#post1005938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say a circle of Solars somehow gets in good with Lunars of the Winding Path and try to support their efforts to build societies that can survive and thrive without the Exalted: how does that play out? What kind of society would a Solar/Lunar collaboration produce?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, it's going to change completely depending on which Solar and which Lunar are working together. Solar and Lunar kingdoms are going to be reflections of that particular Solar or Lunar, their beliefs, where they were raised, what they think, etc. <br /> <br /> If Strength-of-Many and Panther teamed up to make a kingdom, it would be completely different from a kingdom created by the joint efforts of Leviathan and Lyta or the kind of nightmarish hell-on-earth if Raksi and Filial Wisdom decided to work together to create a kingdom.<br /> <br /> So the most important thing is to first consider which Lunar and which Solar you're looking at - because, I'm fairly sure my Raksi/Filial Wisdom cannibal bromance paradise is going to be a bit different than what other people imagine a Lunar/Solar teamup would look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T15:12:31-08:00","id":1006873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1005938-solars-the-thousand-streams-river?p=1006860#post1006860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar and Lunar kingdoms are going to be reflections of that particular Solar or Lunar, their beliefs, where they were raised, what they think, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, they're probably also going to be defined a bit by the people who actually come from there.<br /> <br /> \u200bEven Manual: Lunars didn't make the mistake of portraying the people in places or tribes that the Lunars intersected with as blank canvases, and even portrayed some issues arising from disputes between the values and priorities of the people and their Lunar that were probably more sophisticated than &quot;get sufficiently high social success to make everybody sit down and shut up&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}